etymology_text:
From Proto-Turkic *čöp (“garbage”).
Compare with
Karakhanid [script needed] (čöp, “refuse, residue”);
Kazakh шөп (šöp, “weed; hay”);
Uzbek choʻp (“twig; dry grass”);
Turkmen çöp (“splinter; small stick”);
Turkish çöp (“garbage; small thin branch of grass or tree”),
Khakas сӧп (söp, “garbage”).
